  "id": "t05-005",
  "track": "track-05",
  "title": "ASP.NET Core authentication handlers identity and policies",
  "status": "source-backed-scope-complete",
  "concepts": [
    "ASP.NET Core schemes map named credential sources to handlers. Authentication middleware creates or restores a ClaimsPrincipal; endpoint metadata and authorization middleware evaluate policy requirements.",
    "Cookie authentication, bearer-token validation, and external OIDC sign-in have different trust and redirect behaviors. A JWT handler validates tokens; it is not the same as participating in an OIDC browser sign-in flow.",
    "Policies combine requirements and handlers. Resource-based checks run after a resource is loaded so authorization can evaluate ownership and tenant boundaries.",
    "Middleware order, default schemes, challenge versus forbid, ticket expiration, and secure cookie settings affect runtime behavior and must be configured deliberately."
  ],
